<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    HotPath (C125) — the lightweight production replica's Container 6.

    `specs/lightweight-production-replica.md` §"Container 6 — hot-path" co-locates four logical
    services in ONE .NET process to stay inside the 24 GB VPS budget: mqtt-bridge,
    position-processor-svc, persistence-writer-svc and fleet-health-svc. This project is that
    process, and it contains no domain logic of its own — every one of the four is built by its own
    `XApplication.Build`, exactly as it is in production, and this host only decides where they
    listen and in what order they start and stop.

    WHY IT EXISTS AT ALL, AND WHY SO LATE. `infra/docker-compose.dev.yml` has referenced
    `backend/src/HotPath/Dockerfile` since C009 and nothing ever created it — the C040 handoff
    records it as "still nobody's". C118 went PARTIAL because the dev stack could not be brought up
    without it and deferred it to "C124/C125"; C124 then built 34 per-service images for the D7' §5
    Kubernetes layout, where each of these four IS its own Deployment. So the co-located form the
    replica needs has never existed, and C125 is the first component that cannot proceed without it.

    THE REPLICA'S LAYOUT IS NOT PRODUCTION'S, AND THAT IS THE SPEC'S CHOICE. The same four services
    are four independently-scaled pods under `infra/k8s/base/services/`. The spec's own warning is
    worth repeating here because this file is what implements the trade: co-locating them shares one
    thread pool and one GC heap, so a stall in any one — position-processor on a slow anti-spoof
    check, persistence-writer blocking on a Postgres write spike — pauses the entire hot path.
    Backpressure isolation is sacrificed deliberately, and ADD §3.2's SLOs should be validated on
    the replica under a simulated Postgres slowdown before treating it as launch-equivalent.

    Verify: `infra/replica/deploy.sh` with the dry-run flag. (Written out rather than pasted: an XML
    comment cannot carry a double hyphen, the same reason HotPath.PositionProcessor.csproj spells its
    test filter out. The runnable form is in build/prompts/C125.md and infra/replica/README.md.)
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.HotPath.Host</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MageRide.HotPath</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <UserSecretsId>mageride-hotpath-host</UserSecretsId>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The four services of Container 6. No MageRide.Shared reference: each of these already carries
      it, and naming it here would let this host drift onto a different version of the kernel than
      the services it starts.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\HotPath.MqttBridge\HotPath.MqttBridge.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\HotPath.PositionProcessor\HotPath.PositionProcessor.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\HotPath.PersistenceWriter\HotPath.PersistenceWriter.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\FleetHealth\FleetHealth.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
